# generation: 1
# The only place a PVE node name becomes an address. PVE stores container
# configs under /etc/pve/nodes/<name>/, so the name is unavoidable - resolving
# it is not. This machine is outside the cluster and has neither its hosts file
# nor its DNS, so every address it will ever use is in this table.
#
# TAB separated; lines starting with # are ignored. role is one of:
#   storage   the node the engines run on, and where the images live
#   backup    holds the stopped DR copies, and PBS
#   compute   mounts the images over NFS and runs the containers
#
# name	ip	role
pve-storage-r17	10.100.1.17	storage
pbs-r09	10.100.1.9	backup
pve-r32	10.100.1.32	compute
pve-r33	10.100.1.33	compute
